<title>USA: U.S. crop production Oct 11 highlights - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. crop production Oct 11 highlights - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA Friday raised its 1996 corn crop estimate to 9.012 billion bushels and soybeans to 2.346 billion bushels, and lowered wheat to 2.282 billion.</p>
<p>A month ago, USDA estimated the corn crop at 8.804 billion bushels, soybeans at 2.270 billion, and wheat at 2.296 billion.</p>
<p>It revised last year's soybean crop to 2.177 billion bushels from 2.152 billion, and wheat to 2.183 billion from 2.186 billion. The corn crop was 7.374 billion bushels last year.</p>
<p>Analyst estimates for corn production averaged 8.951 billion bushels and for soybeans 2.287 billion.  </p>
